# Dependencies land here when the package is developed standalone.
node_modules/

# The journal is the one ledger file that does NOT travel with the project.
#
# `DESIGN.md` §2.1 has said so since the beginning — "只有 journal.jsonl 排除在外，它是每次验证
# 追加一行的机器写入流，进 git 只会让每次验证都产生一条 diff" — but until 2026-10-04 nothing
# enforced it, because the package had no repository to enforce it in. Measured at the first
# commit: journal.jsonl 133 KB + .000 513 KB + .001 516 KB, i.e. the append-only machine stream
# was about to become 85% of the repository. The rotated segments are generated by
# `rotateJournal` (rename only, never delete), so they are regenerated locally and must not be
# tracked either.
.dsh-code/journal.jsonl
.dsh-code/journal.jsonl.*
# The machine-wide ledger lives in `~/.dsh-code/` and can never be inside this repository, so
# it needs no rule here — noted so the next reader does not add one that silently never fires.

# Probe scratch and reports: regenerated by the probes themselves.
# Scratch fixtures no longer land here — since 2026-10-02 they are created under
# the OS temp dir (os.tmpdir()), because a sandboxed channel cannot write a
# pre-existing subdirectory of the workspace. The four fixture lines are kept so
# checkouts that still carry the old files do not show them as untracked.
probes/budget-small.txt
probes/budget-large.txt
probes/budget-dir/
probes/budget-missing-does-not-exist.txt
probes/budget-log.txt
probes/budget-report.json
probes/budget-report.md
probes/standard.patch.yml
# `probes/handover-debug-scratch.mjs` used to be listed here as a leftover a confined session
# could not delete. It was deleted on 2026-10-04 in an unrestricted channel, and an ignore rule
# for a file that does not exist is a claim about the tree that quietly stops being true. The
# two new probes (`pattern-budget-probe`, `repeat-identity-probe`) keep their scratch under
# os.tmpdir(), so nothing here needs to grow for them.
